  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 1232 PM CDT Wed Apr 22 2026\n\nLooks like a mainly hot and dry forecast through next week across \nthe area as 500 MB heights rise and a low level thermal ridge sets \nup close to our area. Also, a dryline will be near or just west \nof the area and slosh back/forth through next week. Development of\nconvection along the dryline is very conditional for the next 7 \ndays as a strong cap will be in place. Sunday may be the best  \nday for isolated thunderstorm activity. Any storm that develops \nwill become severe due to extreme instability and some deep layer\nshear. The better chance of organized severe weather will be to \nour north. For our area, the severe weather risk is very low to \nlow(2 to 14 percent) in the long term. Keep up with the latest \nweather information as the month of April is severe weather \nseason. Highs will mainly be in the upper 80s and 90s. Also, it \nwill be humid mainly during the overnight and morning hours.",
